How to create a site skin with this code:
> Dashboard
> Skins
> Create Site Skin
> Fill out relevant information and boxes
    - Make sure it's set to "Write Custom CSS"
    - Type Should be Site Skin, unless I make work skins in the future
    - Give unique name. Can be keysmash.
    - Paste code. Make sure you select and paste ALL of the code, even commentary (the 'brackets' prevent it from causing an error, I believe.)
> Submit and start using!

////

Add-Ons: How to Use
You can just add the code onto a site skin you're using, but it'll be better housekeeping to do this and allow yourself to apply add-ons to any skin (even if they need to be adjusted to fit aesthetically).
> Create a skin with the add-on code
> Go to the main skin and edit
> Scroll to the bottom and show Advanced
> Add parent skin
> Type/paste the name you gave the add-on skin code
> Submit and start using!

